doctype html
html(lang='en')
  head
    meta(charset='utf-8')
    meta(name='viewport' content='width=device-width, initial-scale=1')
    meta(name='csrf-token' content=csrfToken)
    title Import AmiAmi items
    link(rel='stylesheet' href='/css/color-theme.css')
    link(rel='stylesheet' href='/css/amiami-upload.css')
    script(src='/js/amiami-upload.js' defer)
    include includes/navigation_assets
  body
    include includes/navigation
    main
      nav(aria-label='Navigation')
        a(href='/admin') Administration
        a(href='/admin/amiami-items') AmiAmi items
      header
        p.eyebrow AmiAmi catalog
        h1 Import item list
        p Upload or paste HTML copied from your browser, or a prepared list with one item code per line. For HTML, a whole page, a container or a single item link will work.
      p#upload-status(role='status' aria-live='polite') Checking for a previous import…
      noscript This form needs JavaScript to upload a list and display progress.
      section#job-panel(hidden aria-labelledby='job-heading')
        .heading-row
          h2#job-heading Import progress
          span#job-state.badge
        p#job-message
        progress#job-progress(max='1' value='0')
        p#job-summary
        dl.stats
          div
            dt Item codes
            dd#job-total 0
          div
            dt Skipped records
            dd#job-existing 0
          div
            dt Fetched
            dd#job-fetched 0
          div
            dt Failed
            dd#job-failed 0
        p#job-timing
        p#job-current
        p#job-skipped-errors
        p#background-note You can close this page. The import continues in the background; reopen it to see progress or add more items to the shared queue.
        details#failure-panel(hidden)
          summary Items that could not be fetched
          ul#job-failures
        p.job-reference#job-reference
      section#upload-panel(hidden aria-labelledby='upload-heading')
        h2#upload-heading Add an item list
        p Add items at any time, including while an import is running. New items go to the end of the shared queue. Existing records and codes already queued are skipped. Items are fetched one at a time, with a 60-second pause after each attempt.
        form#upload-form
          label(for='input-format') Input format
          select#input-format
            option(value='html') HTML
            option(value='codes') Item codes (one per line)
          label#file-label(for='html-file') Upload a saved HTML file
          input#html-file(type='file' accept='.html,.htm,text/html')
          p.or Or paste below
          label#input-label(for='html-input') HTML fragment or document
          textarea#html-input(rows='10' spellcheck='false' placeholder='<a href="/eng/detail?gcode=TOY-RBT-9417">…</a>')
          p.help#format-help HTML is parsed as text and discarded; it is never displayed or executed.
          p.help Up to 2 MiB of UTF-8 text and 1,000 distinct item codes per upload. The queue holds up to 1,000 pending items, including possible size fallbacks. Duplicates are skipped.
          p.help Codes ending in -Rxxx, -Sxxx or -Dxxx (three digits) use the base item code. If the base lookup fails, each original -Sxxx code gets one attempt in case it identifies a clothing size.
          label
            input#retry-failed(type='checkbox')
            |  Retry empty records from failed lookups in this list
          p.help Before retrying, check that these item codes still open on AmiAmi. Each selected placeholder gets one attempt; records with fetched details are preserved.
          button#upload-submit(type='submit') Start import
      button#refresh-status.secondary(type='button') Refresh status
